      "important_limitations": [
        "OTTS field 50 is engine make/type, not a confirmed VAG factory engine code.",
        "OTTS fields 14-18 identify make, commercial name, type, base vehicle/chassis and modifications; they do not establish exact engine/gearbox fitment by themselves.",
        "OTTS field 40 contains VINs covered by the approval; field 79 describes VIN structure.",
        "The OTTS attribute list does not provide a dedicated gearbox-code field.",
        "SBKTS Appendix 1 field 68 is gearbox make/type, but SBKTS is an individual-vehicle safety certificate, not an OTTS type-approval record.",
        "Do not use SBKTS personal data or package certificate PDFs without separate rights and privacy review.",
        "The existing ot_ts_attribute_map uses Annex 1 internal FGIS field numbers. Public-site search fields are a separate Annex 2 namespace; never join or interpret them by field number without the namespace.",
        "The 28 public Annex 2 search fields contain approval identifiers/status and vehicle identity descriptors (make, commercial name, type, base vehicle/chassis, modifications, category and environmental class), but no engine or gearbox technical designation/code, ECU, DTC, repair or wiring fields. The Annex 1 PDF reference is not a grant to cache or redistribute the PDF. Never infer an engine/gearbox pair from Annex 2 metadata.",
        "The Annex 2 public-site search obligation reviewed in Order 2038 applies to electronically issued records; a metadata export using this public-search namespace must retain field 20 and must not silently treat a missing/false electronic-issuance flag as a publicly searchable record.",
        "Interstandart's registry-software FAQ describes a formal application for accredited certification bodies or testing laboratories and requires licensed IBM/HCL Domino. The main FAQ lists TR TS 018/2011, while consolidated page text also lists GOST 33670; eligibility wording is inconsistent and requires written clarification. This software-access procedure is not a data-reuse license."
      ],
